1
00:00:01,168 --> 00:00:02,127
PHEEBS, CAN YOU
HELP ME PICK OUT

2
00:00:02,127 --> 00:00:03,211
AN ENGAGEMENT RING
FOR MONICA?

3
00:00:03,211 --> 00:00:05,005
I CAN'T FIGURE THIS OUT.
IT'S SO HARD.

4
00:00:05,005 --> 00:00:09,301
SHOULD I GET HER A TIFFANY CUT
OR A PRINCESS CUT OR A... OW!

5
00:00:09,301 --> 00:00:11,428
PAPER CUT!

6
00:00:11,428 --> 00:00:12,847
NOW, HAVE YOU TOLD
ANYONE ELSE?

7
00:00:12,847 --> 00:00:14,348
NO. I DON'T WANT
TO TELL ANYBODY ELSE

8
00:00:14,348 --> 00:00:16,099
BECAUSE I DON'T WANT
MONICA TO FIND OUT.

9
00:00:16,099 --> 00:00:17,392
YOU TOLD ME.

10
00:00:17,392 --> 00:00:18,811
WELL, THAT'S BECAUSE
I TRUST YOU

11
00:00:18,811 --> 00:00:20,103
AND YOU'RE ONE OF
MY BEST FRIENDS

12
00:00:20,103 --> 00:00:21,480
AND YOU WALKED
IN ON ME

13
00:00:21,480 --> 00:00:24,232
WHILE I WAS LOOKING
AT RING BROCHURES.

14
00:00:24,232 --> 00:00:27,444
YEAH, WELL, ONCE AGAIN,
NOT KNOCKING PAYS OFF.

15
00:00:27,444 --> 00:00:29,237
I ONLY WISH YOU HADN'T
BEEN ON THE TOILET.

16
00:00:29,237 --> 00:00:32,658
ME, TOO.

17
00:00:32,658 --> 00:00:34,201
HEY.
HEY.
HEY.

18
00:00:34,201 --> 00:00:35,494
SO, CHANDLER, WANT TO
GO TO THE COFFEE HOUSE?

19
00:00:35,494 --> 00:00:37,538
OH, ALL RIGHT.
YEAH, COFFEE HOUSE.

20
00:00:37,538 --> 00:00:40,081
PERFECT. WE WERE JUST GOING
TO SEE IF YOU WANTED TO GO.

21
00:00:40,081 --> 00:00:42,292
OH, WELL, WE DON'T
'CAUSE WE GOT THE OTHER PLACE.

22
00:00:46,505 --> 00:00:49,299
HOW RUDE.

23
00:00:49,299 --> 00:00:51,134
OH, I'M SORRY.
YOU WANT A BITE?

24
00:00:56,932 --> 00:01:03,188
♪ SO NO ONE TOLD YOU
LIFE WAS GONNA BE THIS WAY ♪

25
00:01:03,188 --> 00:01:05,691
♪ YOUR JOB'S A JOKE,
YOU'RE BROKE ♪

26
00:01:05,691 --> 00:01:08,276
♪ YOUR LOVE LIFE'S D.O.A. ♪

27
00:01:08,276 --> 00:01:12,447
♪ IT'S LIKE YOU'RE ALWAYS
STUCK IN SECOND GEAR ♪

28
00:01:12,447 --> 00:01:15,116
♪ WHEN IT HASN'T BEEN
YOUR DAY, YOUR WEEK ♪

29
00:01:15,116 --> 00:01:17,745
♪ YOUR MONTH,
OR EVEN YOUR YEAR ♪

30
00:01:17,745 --> 00:01:21,749
♪ BUT I'LL BE THERE FOR YOU ♪

31
00:01:21,749 --> 00:01:26,045
♪ 'CAUSE YOU'RE THERE
FOR ME, TOO. ♪

32
00:01:31,633 --> 00:01:34,386
SO HOW ARE THINGS
GOING WITH PAUL?

33
00:01:34,386 --> 00:01:35,804
GOOD.

34
00:01:35,804 --> 00:01:37,973
ALTHOUGH, YOU KNOW,
HE'S A PRIVATE GUY.

35
00:01:37,973 --> 00:01:39,307
YOU KNOW, I WISH
I COULD GET HIM

36
00:01:39,307 --> 00:01:41,769
TO OPEN UP A LITTLE BIT,
SHARE SOME FEELINGS.

37
00:01:41,769 --> 00:01:43,938
THAT'S EASY.
YOU JUST HAVE TO THINK OF HIM

38
00:01:43,938 --> 00:01:47,942
AS A JAR OF PICKLES
THAT WON'T OPEN.

39
00:01:47,942 --> 00:01:49,359
SO WHAT ARE YOU SAYING?

40
00:01:49,359 --> 00:01:50,652
I SHOULD RUN HIM
UNDER SOME HOT WATER

41
00:01:50,652 --> 00:01:53,989
AND BANG HIS HEAD
AGAINST THE TABLE?

42
00:01:53,989 --> 00:01:55,616
NO. THAT'S WHAT YOU DO
WHEN YOU WANT TO GET

43
00:01:55,616 --> 00:01:56,742
THE TRUTH OUT OF SOMEONE.

44
00:01:56,742 --> 00:01:58,452
( chuckles )

45
00:02:01,204 --> 00:02:02,456
HI, HONEY.
HI.

46
00:02:02,456 --> 00:02:03,457
WATCH THIS.

47
00:02:03,457 --> 00:02:04,792
OKAY.

48
00:02:04,792 --> 00:02:06,085
HEY, PAUL.
HI, PHOEBE.

49
00:02:06,085 --> 00:02:09,755
SO, HOW ARE THINGS
GOING WITH YOU?

50
00:02:09,755 --> 00:02:11,966
CAN'T COMPLAIN.

51
00:02:11,966 --> 00:02:14,301
( clucks tongue )

52
00:02:16,428 --> 00:02:17,429
LET'S GO.
OKAY.

53
00:02:17,429 --> 00:02:19,014
HEY!
HI!

54
00:02:19,014 --> 00:02:20,265
ROSS, GOOD
TO SEE YOU, TOO.

55
00:02:20,265 --> 00:02:22,267
HOW YOU DOING?
GOOD. BYE.

56
00:02:22,267 --> 00:02:24,061
OKAY, YOU TAKE CARE.

57
00:02:24,061 --> 00:02:25,062
YEAH!

58
00:02:25,062 --> 00:02:26,563
EW.

59
00:02:29,024 --> 00:02:30,525
HEY, PHEEBS, WHAT WAS THE DEAL

60
00:02:30,525 --> 00:02:32,861
WITH YOU AND CHANDLER
BLOWING US OFF BEFORE?

61
00:02:32,861 --> 00:02:36,364
YEAH, IT WAS SO WEIRD, HUH?

62
00:02:36,364 --> 00:02:37,658
PHOEBE, WHY'D YOU DO IT?

63
00:02:37,658 --> 00:02:39,284
I DIDN'T DO IT.

64
00:02:39,284 --> 00:02:40,911
IT WAS CHANDLER.

65
00:02:40,911 --> 00:02:43,038
HE'S... HE'S MAD AT YOU.

66
00:02:43,038 --> 00:02:45,082
WHA...? WHY?

67
00:02:45,082 --> 00:02:48,085
PLEASE. I THINK YOU KNOW WHY.

68
00:02:48,085 --> 00:02:50,420
CAN'T THINK OF ANYTHING.

69
00:02:50,420 --> 00:02:51,421
COME ON, ROSS.

70
00:02:51,421 --> 00:02:52,464
YOU'RE A PALEONTOLOGIST.

71
00:02:52,464 --> 00:02:54,382
DIG A LITTLE DEEPER.

72
00:02:56,969 --> 00:02:58,512
WAIT A MINUTE.
IS IT 'CAUSE JOEY AND I

73
00:02:58,512 --> 00:02:59,972
DIDN'T INVITE HIM
TO THAT KNICKS GAME

74
00:02:59,972 --> 00:03:01,849
A COUPLE OF WEEKS AGO?

75
00:03:01,849 --> 00:03:05,686
DO YOU THINK THAT'S SOMETHING
THAT HE'D BE MAD AT YOU FOR?

76
00:03:05,686 --> 00:03:07,062
I GUESS IT COULD.

77
00:03:07,062 --> 00:03:09,188
WELL, THEN, I THINK THAT'S IT.

78
00:03:09,188 --> 00:03:10,649
WELL, IF HE'S ANGRY

79
00:03:10,649 --> 00:03:12,567
HE REALLY SHOULDN'T
JUST COVER IT UP.

80
00:03:12,567 --> 00:03:14,069
I WISH HE WOULD
JUST TELL ME THE TRUTH.

81
00:03:14,069 --> 00:03:15,529
OH, IF THAT'S WHAT YOU WANT

82
00:03:15,529 --> 00:03:17,447
THEN YOU REALLY SHOULD
RUN HIM UNDER HOT WATER

83
00:03:17,447 --> 00:03:20,325
AND BANG HIS HEAD
AGAINST THE TABLE.

84
00:03:22,577 --> 00:03:24,496
HONEY, I MADE A RESERVATION
AT CHINA GARDEN.

85
00:03:24,496 --> 00:03:25,539
IS THAT OKAY?

86
00:03:25,539 --> 00:03:27,206
YEAH. NO, THAT'S GREAT.

87
00:03:27,206 --> 00:03:29,208
BUT FIRST, WAIT.
TALK TO ME, TALK TO ME.

88
00:03:29,208 --> 00:03:32,211
TELL ME ABOUT YOUR DAY.

89
00:03:32,211 --> 00:03:34,173
IT WAS FINE.

90
00:03:35,340 --> 00:03:37,718
OKAY.
( chuckles )

91
00:03:37,718 --> 00:03:40,095
HEY, WHAT ARE YOU THINKING
RIGHT NOW?

92
00:03:40,095 --> 00:03:42,723
I'M THINKING
THAT YOU ARE LOOKING REALLY FINE

93
00:03:42,723 --> 00:03:45,017
IN THAT DRESS.

94
00:03:45,017 --> 00:03:46,351
YOU KNOW, THAT'S
GREAT, PAUL

95
00:03:46,351 --> 00:03:50,105
BUT YOU KNOW,
I WANT TO KNOW WHAT...

96
00:03:50,105 --> 00:03:52,149
WOW, THOSE ARE
REALLY GREAT.

97
00:03:52,149 --> 00:03:54,359
UM...

98
00:03:54,359 --> 00:03:56,403
UM, I JUST WANT
TO KNOW WHAT IS

99
00:03:56,403 --> 00:04:00,657
BEHIND THIS STRONG,
SILENT EXTERIOR.

100
00:04:00,657 --> 00:04:02,701
YOU KNOW, THEY SAY THAT
STILL WATERS RUN DEEP

101
00:04:02,701 --> 00:04:05,746
AND I WANT TO
SWIM IN YOURS.

102
00:04:07,873 --> 00:04:11,001
ARE YOU TALKING
ABOUT HAVING SEX?

103
00:04:11,001 --> 00:04:14,337
NO. PAUL, I DON'T KNOW
ANYTHING ABOUT YOU.

104
00:04:14,337 --> 00:04:15,589
YOU KNOW, LIKE
YOUR CHILDHOOD.

105
00:04:15,589 --> 00:04:17,674
TELL ME ABOUT
YOUR CHILDHOOD.

106
00:04:17,674 --> 00:04:19,760
NORMAL.

107
00:04:19,760 --> 00:04:21,595
OKAY. WELL, THEN
HOW ABOUT PUBERTY?

108
00:04:21,595 --> 00:04:23,847
COME ON. THAT'S ALWAYS
A PAINFUL TIME.

109
00:04:23,847 --> 00:04:25,849
YOU KNOW, WHEN YOUR FRIENDS
INVITE YOU TO A SLUMBER PARTY

110
00:04:25,849 --> 00:04:27,935
AND THEN THEY STICK
YOUR HAND IN WARM WATER

111
00:04:27,935 --> 00:04:29,019
WHILE YOU'RE SLEEPING
SO THAT YOU

112
00:04:29,019 --> 00:04:32,814
PEE IN YOUR
SLEEPING BAG?

113
00:04:32,814 --> 00:04:35,525
NOPE, THAT NEVER
HAPPENED TO ME.

114
00:04:35,525 --> 00:04:40,030
WELL, YOU'RE LUCKY YOU NEVER
MET THAT BITCH SHARON MAJESKI.

115
00:04:40,030 --> 00:04:43,200
ANYWAY, UM,
THE REST OF YOUR LIFE.

116
00:04:43,200 --> 00:04:45,452
YOU KNOW, ANY REGRETS?

117
00:04:45,452 --> 00:04:47,913
NOPE.

118
00:04:47,913 --> 00:04:49,123
ALL RIGHT, PAUL.
YOU KNOW, I'M NOT ASKING

119
00:04:49,123 --> 00:04:50,289
FOR A LOT HERE, OKAY?

120
00:04:50,289 --> 00:04:51,583
JUST GIVE ME SOMETHING.

121
00:04:51,583 --> 00:04:54,294
ANYTHING.

122
00:04:54,294 --> 00:04:57,256
OKAY.
OKAY.

123
00:04:58,632 --> 00:05:00,926
WHEN I WAS SIX YEARS OLD...
MM-HMM.

124
00:05:00,926 --> 00:05:03,178
I WANTED A BIG WHEEL.

125
00:05:03,178 --> 00:05:05,097
AND INSTEAD,
MY PARENTS GOT ME

126
00:05:05,097 --> 00:05:09,601
THIS LITTLE PLASTIC
CHICKEN THAT YOU
HOP AROUND ON.

127
00:05:09,601 --> 00:05:11,686
IT WAS EMBARRASSING.

128
00:05:11,686 --> 00:05:13,021
KIDS MADE FUN OF ME.
OH.

129
00:05:13,021 --> 00:05:16,316
THAT WAS A PRETTY
TOUGH YEAR.

130
00:05:16,316 --> 00:05:18,860
THAT'S GREAT. SEE?

131
00:05:18,860 --> 00:05:20,070
I ALREADY FEEL
LIKE I KNOW YOU

132
00:05:20,070 --> 00:05:21,071
A LITTLE BETTER.

133
00:05:21,071 --> 00:05:22,322
THANK YOU.

134
00:05:22,322 --> 00:05:23,657
OKAY. COME ON.
NOW WE CAN GO EAT.

135
00:05:23,657 --> 00:05:25,784
LET'S GO.

136
00:05:28,162 --> 00:05:29,830
IT WAS HORRIBLE.

137
00:05:32,249 --> 00:05:36,003
THEY CALLED ME "CHICKEN BOY."

138
00:05:36,003 --> 00:05:41,883
( sobbing )

139
00:05:41,883 --> 00:05:43,677
AND IN FIFTH GRADE,
I GOT INTO A FIGHT.

140
00:05:43,677 --> 00:05:45,512
WELL, IT WASN'T REALLY A FIGHT.

141
00:05:45,512 --> 00:05:48,890
RICHARD DARUMBULL BIT ME
ON THE NOSE AND I FELL DOWN.

142
00:05:48,890 --> 00:05:49,975
I STILL HAVE A LITTLE SCAR
RIGHT HERE.

143
00:05:49,975 --> 00:05:51,518
YOU CAN SEE IT.

144
00:05:51,518 --> 00:05:53,687
YEAH, I SEE THE SCAR.

145
00:05:53,687 --> 00:05:57,024
LISTEN, PAUL, I THINK
THIS IS REALLY GREAT

146
00:05:57,024 --> 00:05:59,067
THAT, YOU KNOW, YOU'VE
SHARED YOUR FEELINGS.

147
00:05:59,067 --> 00:06:00,819
IT'S REALLY BEAUTIFUL

148
00:06:00,819 --> 00:06:04,531
BUT, UM, WHAT DO YOU SAY
WE GO SHARE SOME FOOD?

149
00:06:04,531 --> 00:06:06,449
OH, I COULDN'T EAT NOW.

150
00:06:06,449 --> 00:06:08,202
WHAT ARE YOU TALKING ABOUT?

151
00:06:08,202 --> 00:06:12,039
YOU LOVE
THEIR KUNG PAO CHICKEN.

152
00:06:12,039 --> 00:06:13,581
"CHICKEN"?

153
00:06:16,335 --> 00:06:17,376
"CHICKEN BOY!"

154
00:06:17,376 --> 00:06:18,377
I'M SORRY! I'M SORRY.

155
00:06:18,377 --> 00:06:19,587
I DIDN'T MEAN TO DO THIS.

156
00:06:19,587 --> 00:06:22,341
( mimics clucking )

157
00:06:27,637 --> 00:06:29,639
THIS IS THE NINE MILLIONTH
RING STORE WE'VE BEEN TO

158
00:06:29,639 --> 00:06:31,892
AND I CAN'T FIND
THE PERFECT RING.

159
00:06:31,892 --> 00:06:34,519
UGLY RING, UGLY RING,
UGLY RING.

160
00:06:38,148 --> 00:06:40,317
IT'S A BEAUTIFUL SELECTION.

161
00:06:41,902 --> 00:06:44,196
OKAY, SO MAYBE YOU
DON'T GET HER A RING.

162
00:06:44,196 --> 00:06:45,780
MAYBE YOU DO SOMETHING
DIFFERENT.

163
00:06:45,780 --> 00:06:47,074
YOU KNOW, MAYBE
YOU GET HER

164
00:06:47,074 --> 00:06:48,616
AN ENGAGEMENT
BRACELET, YOU KNOW?

165
00:06:48,616 --> 00:06:50,869
OR AN ENGAGEMENT TIARA.

166
00:06:50,869 --> 00:06:56,124
OH, AN ENGAGEMENT
REVOLUTIONARY WAR MUSKET.

167
00:06:56,124 --> 00:06:59,753
YOU KNOW, I'M SO GLAD I PICKED
YOU TO HELP ME WITH THIS.
HUH?

168
00:06:59,753 --> 00:07:02,047
CAN'T YOU JUST IMAGINE
GETTING DOWN ON ONE KNEE

169
00:07:02,047 --> 00:07:06,343
AND HANDING HER THIS
GORGEOUS PIECE OF WEAPONRY?

170
00:07:06,343 --> 00:07:08,387
YEAH, I'M GOING
TO STICK WITH THE RING.

171
00:07:10,222 --> 00:07:11,223
OH, THIS ONE'S NICE.

172
00:07:11,223 --> 00:07:12,224
I LIKE THIS ONE.

173
00:07:12,224 --> 00:07:13,474
SIR, UH, KIND SIR.

174
00:07:13,474 --> 00:07:15,435
CAN I SEE THIS ONE?

175
00:07:15,435 --> 00:07:18,105
WAIT A MINUTE.
THIS IS THE REASON
YOU BROUGHT ME, OKAY?

176
00:07:18,105 --> 00:07:19,522
I KNOW HOW TO HAGGLE

177
00:07:19,522 --> 00:07:21,441
SO LET ME HANDLE THIS
FROM HERE ON OUT.

178
00:07:21,441 --> 00:07:22,901
CAN I HELP YOU?
UH, YES.

179
00:07:22,901 --> 00:07:24,861
I WOULD LIKE TO SEE
THAT RING, PLEASE.

180
00:07:24,861 --> 00:07:27,989
OR NOT. WHATEVER.

181
00:07:27,989 --> 00:07:29,783
THIS RING IS
FROM THE 1920s.

182
00:07:29,783 --> 00:07:31,659
IT'S A 1h-CARAT DIAMOND

183
00:07:31,659 --> 00:07:33,620
WITH SAPPHIRES
ON EITHER SIDE.

184
00:07:33,620 --> 00:07:35,330
SIR, COULD I ASK
YOU TO, UM

185
00:07:35,330 --> 00:07:41,460
COULD YOU HOLD OUT THAT RING
AND ASK ME TO MARRY YOU?

186
00:07:41,460 --> 00:07:43,130
OKAY.

187
00:07:45,006 --> 00:07:47,550
WILL YOU MARRY ME?

188
00:07:47,550 --> 00:07:51,305
OH, MY GOD. THAT'S IT.
THAT'S THE RING.

189
00:07:51,305 --> 00:07:53,932
HOW MUCH IS IT?
CHANDLER,
I WILL HANDLE THIS.

190
00:07:53,932 --> 00:07:56,351
HOW MUCH IS IT?

191
00:07:56,351 --> 00:07:58,019
$8,600.

192
00:07:58,019 --> 00:08:01,940
WE WILL GIVE YOU
TEN DOLLARS.

193
00:08:01,940 --> 00:08:03,400
ARE YOU INTERESTED
IN THIS RING?

194
00:08:03,400 --> 00:08:07,570
YES. YES, BUT I CAN
ONLY PAY $8,000.

195
00:08:07,570 --> 00:08:08,905
OKAY. I CAN LET IT
GO FOR $8,000.

196
00:08:08,905 --> 00:08:11,825
WE STAND FIRM
AT TEN DOLLARS.

197
00:08:11,825 --> 00:08:12,826
HOW WOULD YOU
LIKE TO PAY?

198
00:08:12,826 --> 00:08:14,328
UH, CREDIT CARD.

199
00:08:14,328 --> 00:08:16,663
OH, NO. BUT I LENT
MY CREDIT CARD TO JOEY.

200
00:08:16,663 --> 00:08:17,705
OKAY, I'LL GO GET IT.

201
00:08:17,705 --> 00:08:18,706
YOU GUARD THE RING.

202
00:08:18,706 --> 00:08:21,209
OKAY.

203
00:08:21,209 --> 00:08:23,711
LISTEN, I'M SORRY
ABOUT BEFORE.

204
00:08:23,711 --> 00:08:26,256
DO YOU HAVE ANYTHING
HERE FOR TEN DOLLARS?

205
00:08:26,256 --> 00:08:28,216
UH, YES.
I HAVE THESE TWO

206
00:08:28,216 --> 00:08:34,055
RATHER BEAUTIFUL
FIVE DOLLAR BILLS.

207
00:08:34,055 --> 00:08:36,475
I'LL GIVE YOU
ONE DOLLAR FOR THEM.

208
00:08:39,019 --> 00:08:40,561
HEY, REMEMBER HOW
CHANDLER AND PHOEBE

209
00:08:40,561 --> 00:08:42,689
BLEW US OFF YESTERDAY?

210
00:08:42,689 --> 00:08:45,025
NO.

211
00:08:45,025 --> 00:08:47,694
REMEMBER? YOU WERE
EATING PIZZA.
YEAH.

212
00:08:47,694 --> 00:08:50,071
OKAY.

213
00:08:50,071 --> 00:08:51,781
WELL, APPARENTLY,
CHANDLER'S ANGRY AT US

214
00:08:51,781 --> 00:08:53,450
FOR NOT GETTING
HIM A TICKET

215
00:08:53,450 --> 00:08:55,076
TO THAT KNICKS GAME
A COUPLE OF WEEKS AGO.

216
00:08:55,076 --> 00:08:57,662
WE WERE SUPPOSED
TO JUST GET HIM A TICKET?

217
00:08:57,662 --> 00:08:59,664
THAT GUY IS
ALWAYS MOOCHING OFF OF US.

218
00:08:59,664 --> 00:09:02,167
RIGHT.

219
00:09:02,167 --> 00:09:04,878
ANYWAY, I STILL THINK WE SHOULD
TRY TO PATCH THINGS UP.

220
00:09:04,878 --> 00:09:06,338
YOU KNOW, LIKE, UH...

221
00:09:06,338 --> 00:09:08,715
MAYBE WE CAN GET HIM TICKETS
TO ANOTHER KNICKS GAME

222
00:09:08,715 --> 00:09:11,009
AND INVITE HIM.
OH, WOW, THAT'S
A GREAT IDEA.

223
00:09:11,009 --> 00:09:13,887
AND I STILL HAVE
HIS CREDIT CARD.

224
00:09:13,887 --> 00:09:14,929
HERE YOU GO.

225
00:09:14,929 --> 00:09:16,097
HEY, HEY, HEY.
HOLD ON.

226
00:09:16,097 --> 00:09:19,059
I GOT THIS ONE.
HERE YOU GO.

227
00:09:19,059 --> 00:09:20,394
YOU KNOW,
I GOT TO TELL YOU.

228
00:09:20,394 --> 00:09:22,270
SOMETIMES
I DON'T GET CHANDLER.

229
00:09:22,270 --> 00:09:23,730
YOU KNOW, ME AND
HIM DO STUFF

230
00:09:23,730 --> 00:09:24,981
ALL THE TIME WITHOUT YOU

231
00:09:24,981 --> 00:09:27,234
AND YOU DON'T GET
ALL UPSET.

232
00:09:29,610 --> 00:09:30,820
ALL THE TIME?

233
00:09:30,820 --> 00:09:32,906
ALL THE TIME.

234
00:09:34,199 --> 00:09:37,494
OH, MY GOD! OH, MY GOD!

235
00:09:37,494 --> 00:09:38,786
STILL CRYING?

236
00:09:38,786 --> 00:09:42,374
LIKE A LITTLE GIRL.

237
00:09:42,374 --> 00:09:43,875
I KNOW, I KNOW, I KNOW.

238
00:09:43,875 --> 00:09:45,210
THIS IS ALL MY FAULT.

239
00:09:45,210 --> 00:09:47,212
I WANTED HIM TO OPEN UP.

240
00:09:47,212 --> 00:09:49,589
BUT I DIDN'T KNOW
I WAS GOING TO UNLEASH

241
00:09:49,589 --> 00:09:54,428
THIS WEEPY, CLINGY,
MOIST MONSTER.

242
00:09:54,428 --> 00:09:56,430
YOU KNOW, I ONLY KNOW
OF TWO SUREFIRE WAYS

243
00:09:56,430 --> 00:09:59,099
TO SHUT A MAN UP
AND ONE OF THEM IS SEX.

244
00:09:59,099 --> 00:10:00,267
WHAT'S THE OTHER ONE?

245
00:10:00,267 --> 00:10:01,309
I DON'T KNOW. I'VE NEVER HAD

246
00:10:01,309 --> 00:10:03,144
TO USE THE OTHER ONE.

247
00:10:03,144 --> 00:10:04,979
I'M JUST SAYING

248
00:10:04,979 --> 00:10:07,107
YOU KNOW, IF WE'RE HAVING SEX,
HE'S NOT GOING TO BE TALKING.

249
00:10:07,107 --> 00:10:08,108
OH, THAT'S RIGHT.

250
00:10:08,108 --> 00:10:11,111
YOU'RE THE TALKER.

251
00:10:13,738 --> 00:10:15,449
ANYWAY, UH, GREAT IDEA.

252
00:10:15,449 --> 00:10:16,991
UM, I GOT TO GO TO THE STORE.

253
00:10:16,991 --> 00:10:18,701
I TOLD HIM THAT I WOULD BUY HIM
SOME MORE TISSUES.

254
00:10:18,701 --> 00:10:19,702
OH, WE HAVE SOME HERE.

255
00:10:19,702 --> 00:10:20,870
NO, YOU DON'T!

256
00:10:23,582 --> 00:10:28,503
OKAY. UM, I'D ALSO LIKE
TO TRY ON THE TIARA.

257
00:10:30,130 --> 00:10:32,173
OH, YEAH. OKAY.

258
00:10:34,384 --> 00:10:35,718
WOW. WHAT DO YOU THINK?

259
00:10:35,718 --> 00:10:38,179
TOO MUCH?

260
00:10:38,179 --> 00:10:39,347
A TAD.

261
00:10:40,640 --> 00:10:43,017
THEN TAKE THE TIARA BACK

262
00:10:43,017 --> 00:10:47,063
AND LET ME HOLD
THE MUSKET AGAIN.

263
00:10:54,654 --> 00:10:55,947
SOMETHING'S MISSING.

264
00:10:55,947 --> 00:10:57,157
IT'S NOT...

265
00:10:57,157 --> 00:10:58,699
OKAY. OH, LET ME SEE
THE RING

266
00:10:58,699 --> 00:11:01,119
THAT MY FRIEND PICKED OUT.

267
00:11:01,119 --> 00:11:02,203
WHERE'S THE 1920s

268
00:11:02,203 --> 00:11:03,455
PRINCESS-CUT RING?

269
00:11:03,455 --> 00:11:05,873
I JUST SOLD IT
TO THAT GENTLEMAN.

270
00:11:05,873 --> 00:11:07,501
OH, MY GOD!

271
00:11:07,501 --> 00:11:08,502
WAIT! NO!

272
00:11:08,502 --> 00:11:09,586
( alarm blares )

273
00:11:09,586 --> 00:11:12,922
NO! WHAT?! HEY!

274
00:11:12,922 --> 00:11:14,299
LET ME OUT

275
00:11:14,299 --> 00:11:16,551
NOW!

276
00:11:21,889 --> 00:11:23,475
RACHEL?

277
00:11:23,475 --> 00:11:24,767
NO.

278
00:11:24,767 --> 00:11:27,061
HOW ARE YOU, PAUL?

279
00:11:27,061 --> 00:11:28,855
OKAY.

280
00:11:33,318 --> 00:11:35,903
CHANDLER...

281
00:11:35,903 --> 00:11:37,113
DID YOUR DAD EVER HUG YOU?

282
00:11:37,113 --> 00:11:38,114
NO.

283
00:11:38,114 --> 00:11:41,660
DID HE HUG YOU?
NO.

284
00:11:41,660 --> 00:11:43,077
NO, I...

285
00:11:43,077 --> 00:11:46,873
IT'S JUST THAT...
MY DAD NEVER DID.

286
00:11:48,375 --> 00:11:49,668
I MISS MY DAD.

287
00:11:49,668 --> 00:11:51,252
WELL, YOU CAN SEE
MY DAD IN VEGAS

288
00:11:51,252 --> 00:11:53,213
KISSING OTHER DADS.

289
00:11:58,051 --> 00:11:59,052
HEY, CHANDLER?

290
00:11:59,052 --> 00:12:00,428
YEAH?

291
00:12:00,428 --> 00:12:02,222
WOULD YOU...

292
00:12:06,893 --> 00:12:09,437
WOULD YOU HUG ME?

293
00:12:09,437 --> 00:12:11,481
I'M A LITTLE BUSY HERE, PAUL.

294
00:12:11,481 --> 00:12:14,609
( crying ):
THAT'S EXACTLY WHAT
MY DAD USED TO SAY.

295
00:12:14,609 --> 00:12:15,818
OKAY, A QUICK ONE.

296
00:12:15,818 --> 00:12:17,529
COME ON,
HUG IT OUT.

297
00:12:17,529 --> 00:12:19,614
HEY!

298
00:12:19,614 --> 00:12:22,283
THERE YOU GO.

299
00:12:22,283 --> 00:12:24,202
OKAY.

300
00:12:24,202 --> 00:12:27,038
FIVE MORE SECONDS.
OKAY!

301
00:12:27,038 --> 00:12:28,039
HEY.

302
00:12:28,039 --> 00:12:29,583
JOEY!

303
00:12:29,583 --> 00:12:31,585
WHAT, HEY, WHAT,
HEY, WHAT... HEY.

304
00:12:34,295 --> 00:12:37,298
HI. PAUL, IS IT?

305
00:12:37,298 --> 00:12:38,799
DO YOU HAVE MY CREDIT CARD?

306
00:12:38,799 --> 00:12:42,887
YEAH, IT'S IN MY...
IN... IN MY POCKET.

307
00:12:45,557 --> 00:12:46,641
MY BACK POCKET!

308
00:12:46,641 --> 00:12:49,269
THANK GOD.

309
00:12:49,269 --> 00:12:50,520
HEY, LISTEN, I
GOT US TICKETS

310
00:12:50,520 --> 00:12:51,646
TO A KNICKS
GAME TONIGHT.

311
00:12:51,646 --> 00:12:52,813
OH, I CAN'T GO.

312
00:12:52,813 --> 00:12:54,357
COME ON,
IT'LL BE FUN.

313
00:12:54,357 --> 00:12:58,861
ME, YOU AND ROSS AND...
PAUL, PROBABLY.

314
00:13:02,823 --> 00:13:03,991
Phoebe:
CHANDLER

315
00:13:03,991 --> 00:13:05,243
I FOUND THE PERFECT RING.

316
00:13:05,243 --> 00:13:06,911
OH, THAT'S-THAT'S PRETTY NICE

317
00:13:06,911 --> 00:13:08,329
BUT I'M GOING TO GO
WITH THE ONE I PICKED FIRST.

318
00:13:08,329 --> 00:13:09,581
OH, WAKE UP,
CHANDLER.

319
00:13:09,581 --> 00:13:10,831
THE ONE YOU PICKED IS GONE.

320
00:13:10,831 --> 00:13:13,251
IT'S OVER!

321
00:13:13,251 --> 00:13:14,669
WHAT?

322
00:13:14,669 --> 00:13:16,254
SOME GUY BOUGHT IT.
I'M SORRY.

323
00:13:16,254 --> 00:13:19,716
I TRIED TO STOP IT,
BUT THEY PUT ME IN JAIL.

324
00:13:19,716 --> 00:13:21,008
THEY PUT YOU IN JAIL?

325
00:13:21,008 --> 00:13:24,220
THE LITTLE JAIL
BETWEEN THE DOORS.

326
00:13:24,220 --> 00:13:26,222
PHOEBE, I ASKED YOU
TO GUARD THE RING.

327
00:13:26,222 --> 00:13:27,515
I KNOW--
I'M SORRY...

328
00:13:27,515 --> 00:13:29,517
BUT, YOU KNOW,
THIS RING IS BETTER

329
00:13:29,517 --> 00:13:31,227
AND MONICA NEVER EVEN SAW
THE OTHER RING.

330
00:13:31,227 --> 00:13:33,480
YEAH, BUT WHEN HE PROPOSED
TO ME WITH THE RING

331
00:13:33,480 --> 00:13:36,775
I GOT... GOOSEBUMPS.

332
00:13:36,775 --> 00:13:37,776
MAYBE IT WAS THE GUY.

333
00:13:37,776 --> 00:13:39,277
IT WAS THE RING.

334
00:13:42,322 --> 00:13:44,532
HEY, SO, UH, WAS HE EXCITED
ABOUT THE TICKETS?

335
00:13:44,532 --> 00:13:46,367
NO.
HE BLEW US OFF.

336
00:13:46,367 --> 00:13:48,869
WHAT?
I KNOW!

337
00:13:48,869 --> 00:13:50,789
I CAN'T BELIEVE IT.

338
00:13:50,789 --> 00:13:53,040
CAN I TELL YOU SOMETHING?

339
00:13:53,040 --> 00:13:57,086
I'M A LITTLE MAD
AT HIM NOW.

340
00:13:57,086 --> 00:13:58,921
CAN I TELL
YOU SOMETHING?

341
00:14:00,548 --> 00:14:04,969
ME, TOO.
YOU KNOW WHAT?

342
00:14:04,969 --> 00:14:07,722
HE DIDN'T WANT TO TALK TO US
ABOUT BEING ANGRY.

343
00:14:07,722 --> 00:14:10,433
WELL, MAYBE WE DON'T TALK
TO HIM AT ALL.

344
00:14:10,433 --> 00:14:12,769
OOH...

345
00:14:12,769 --> 00:14:14,354
FREEZE HIM OUT.
THAT'S RIGHT.

346
00:14:14,354 --> 00:14:16,063
I LIKE IT.
EH? WE'LL SHOW HIM.

347
00:14:16,063 --> 00:14:18,441
FROM NOW ON, IT'S GOING
TO BE JOEY AND ROSS--

348
00:14:18,441 --> 00:14:19,818
BEST FRIENDS.

349
00:14:19,818 --> 00:14:21,235
OKAY.

350
00:14:21,235 --> 00:14:23,988
WE'RE GOING TO BE THE
NEW JOEY AND CHANDLER.

351
00:14:26,240 --> 00:14:27,534
( door opening )

352
00:14:27,534 --> 00:14:29,243
HI. I'M BACK.
HEY, I HAVE

353
00:14:29,243 --> 00:14:30,370
SO MUCH MORE TO TELL YOU.

354
00:14:30,370 --> 00:14:31,621
I'VE WRITTEN IT ALL DOWN.

355
00:14:31,621 --> 00:14:33,540
AH, THAT'S GREAT.

356
00:14:34,999 --> 00:14:37,084
NO, ACTUALLY, THAT'S...

357
00:14:37,084 --> 00:14:39,045
THAT'S GREAT.

358
00:14:39,045 --> 00:14:40,714
THAT'S REALLY GREAT.

359
00:14:40,714 --> 00:14:41,715
YOU KNOW, I GOT
TO TELL YOU

360
00:14:41,715 --> 00:14:44,133
WRITING

361
00:14:44,133 --> 00:14:46,093
GETS ME, UH...

362
00:14:46,093 --> 00:14:48,680
GETS ME KIND OF HOT.

363
00:14:48,680 --> 00:14:49,889
WAIT, WAIT, LISTEN.

364
00:14:49,889 --> 00:14:52,141
LISTEN TO THIS.

365
00:14:52,141 --> 00:14:55,061
YOU KNOW WHAT I WANTED
TO BE WHEN I WAS THAT AGE?

366
00:14:55,061 --> 00:14:57,063
A LOVER?

367
00:14:57,063 --> 00:14:58,064
SURFER.

368
00:14:58,064 --> 00:14:59,524
OH, YEAH?
SURFER?

369
00:14:59,524 --> 00:15:00,983
I WANTED TO BE ONE WITH
THE WAVES, YOU KNOW...

370
00:15:00,983 --> 00:15:02,151
OKAY, HONEY,
HOLD ON REAL QUICK.

371
00:15:02,151 --> 00:15:03,152
HOLD ON A SECOND.

372
00:15:03,152 --> 00:15:04,904
LET ME JUST, UH...

373
00:15:04,904 --> 00:15:07,365
GET A LITTLE MORE
COMFORTABLE, HERE.

374
00:15:07,365 --> 00:15:08,742
OH, WAIT. NOW,
WAIT A SECOND.

375
00:15:08,742 --> 00:15:11,327
THIS ISN'T TOO
REVEALING, IS IT?

376
00:15:11,327 --> 00:15:12,829
NO.

377
00:15:12,829 --> 00:15:16,583
"WHATEVER HAPPENED
TO THAT LITTLE DUDE...

378
00:15:16,583 --> 00:15:18,793
SO FULL OF DREAMS?"

379
00:15:20,795 --> 00:15:25,091
I DON'T CARE ABOUT
THE LITTLE DUDE!

380
00:15:25,091 --> 00:15:27,552
I CAN'T... I CANNOT
LISTEN TO ANY MORE OF THIS.

381
00:15:27,552 --> 00:15:29,136
THE ONLY PERSON
WHO WOULD WANT TO LISTEN

382
00:15:29,136 --> 00:15:31,765
TO ANY MORE OF THIS
IS A MENTAL HEALTH PROFESSIONAL

383
00:15:31,765 --> 00:15:34,141
AND THAT IS ONLY BECAUSE
THEY GET PAID $100 AN HOUR.

384
00:15:34,141 --> 00:15:35,476
DO YOU MUCH HOW MONEY
I COULD HAVE MADE

385
00:15:35,476 --> 00:15:36,603
LISTENING TO YOU?

386
00:15:36,603 --> 00:15:38,646
$2,000.

387
00:15:38,646 --> 00:15:39,980
AND YOU KNOW
WHEN I FIGURED THAT OUT?

388
00:15:39,980 --> 00:15:42,609
WHILE YOU WERE TALKING.

389
00:15:42,609 --> 00:15:44,944
I CAN'T BELIEVE YOU'RE TRYING
TO STIFLE ME

390
00:15:44,944 --> 00:15:47,947
WHEN JUST 14 HOURS AGO, WE
FIGURED OUT THAT THAT IS EXACTLY

391
00:15:47,947 --> 00:15:50,032
WHAT MY MOTHER WAS TRYING
TO DO TO ME.

392
00:15:50,032 --> 00:15:52,326
OH, I'M SORRY.

393
00:15:52,326 --> 00:15:56,289
I... I... I DON'T MEAN...
DIDN'T MEAN TO STIFLE YOU.

394
00:15:56,289 --> 00:16:00,376
I... THIS IS ALL
JUST A LITTLE OVERWHELMING.

395
00:16:00,376 --> 00:16:01,920
OH, RACHEL.

396
00:16:01,920 --> 00:16:02,962
I'M...

397
00:16:02,962 --> 00:16:04,338
SO SORRY.

398
00:16:04,338 --> 00:16:06,173
OH...

399
00:16:06,173 --> 00:16:07,801
I DIDN'T MEAN
TO OVERWHELM YOU.

400
00:16:07,801 --> 00:16:11,596
IT'S JUST THAT...
WHEN THOSE GATES OPENED

401
00:16:11,596 --> 00:16:17,602
IT WAS HARD TO...
HARD TO CLOSE THEM...

402
00:16:17,602 --> 00:16:20,062
BUT THEY ARE CLOSED NOW,
BELIEVE ME.

403
00:16:20,062 --> 00:16:21,188
I'M SO GLAD.

404
00:16:21,188 --> 00:16:24,317
I'M SO GLAD...
YOU SHARED...

405
00:16:24,317 --> 00:16:27,153
AND I'M GLAD
THAT YOU'RE DONE.

406
00:16:29,530 --> 00:16:33,952
SO WHAT DO YOU
SAY WE, UM...

407
00:16:33,952 --> 00:16:35,411
I'D REALLY LIKE THAT.

408
00:16:35,411 --> 00:16:37,204
MM-HMM.

409
00:16:43,127 --> 00:16:44,629
( moans softly )

410
00:16:44,629 --> 00:16:45,713
( sighs )

411
00:16:45,713 --> 00:16:47,089
( moans softly )

412
00:16:47,089 --> 00:16:48,800
THAT WAS...

413
00:16:48,800 --> 00:16:51,177
( crying ):
SO GOOD.

414
00:16:54,639 --> 00:16:56,390
( sobbing )

415
00:16:59,644 --> 00:17:01,103
OH... OH...

416
00:17:01,103 --> 00:17:03,439
YUCK!

417
00:17:03,439 --> 00:17:04,983
HEY.
I CAN'T BELIEVE

418
00:17:04,983 --> 00:17:06,275
I LET YOU TALK ME
INTO BUYING

419
00:17:06,275 --> 00:17:09,236
THIS STUPID,
GUMBALL-MACHINE-LOOKING RING.

420
00:17:09,236 --> 00:17:11,405
IT'S NOT A STUPID,
GUMBALL-MACHINE-
LOOKING RING.

421
00:17:11,405 --> 00:17:12,782
IT'S A BEAUTIFUL RING.

422
00:17:12,782 --> 00:17:14,868
NO, IT'S NOT.

423
00:17:14,868 --> 00:17:16,911
WHEN I LOOKED AT THE OTHER RING
I COULD SEE MONICA'S FACE

424
00:17:16,911 --> 00:17:18,120
WHEN I GAVE IT TO HER,
YOU KNOW?

425
00:17:18,120 --> 00:17:20,247
AND I COULD SEE HER
SAYING, "YES."

426
00:17:20,247 --> 00:17:22,667
WHEN I LOOK AT THIS RING,
ALL I SEE IS A RING...

427
00:17:22,667 --> 00:17:24,084
UNLESS I LOOK AT IT
REALLY CLOSELY

428
00:17:24,084 --> 00:17:28,381
AND THEN...
I CAN SEE MY OWN EYE.

429
00:17:28,381 --> 00:17:31,718
( chuckling )

430
00:17:31,718 --> 00:17:33,761
LOOK, THIS IS
THE MOST IMPORTANT THING

431
00:17:33,761 --> 00:17:35,053
I'M GOING TO DO IN MY LIFE.

432
00:17:35,053 --> 00:17:37,264
I WANT TO MAKE SURE
IT'S PERFECT.

433
00:17:37,264 --> 00:17:38,599
OKAY, THERE MAY BE A WAY

434
00:17:38,599 --> 00:17:40,685
THAT WE COULD GET
THE OTHER RING BACK

435
00:17:40,685 --> 00:17:42,061
'CAUSE I HEARD
THE GUY TELL THE JEWELER

436
00:17:42,061 --> 00:17:43,604
WHERE HE WAS GOING
TO PROPOSE.

437
00:17:43,604 --> 00:17:46,273
SO, MAYBE WE COULD GET HIM
TO TRADE RINGS OR SOMETHING.

438
00:17:46,273 --> 00:17:47,567
WE CAN'T DO THAT.

439
00:17:47,567 --> 00:17:48,568
WELL,
YOU CERTAINLY CAN'T GIVE HER

440
00:17:48,568 --> 00:17:50,987
THAT STUPID
GUMBALL RING.

441
00:17:59,412 --> 00:18:00,955
THERE HE IS.

442
00:18:00,955 --> 00:18:02,498
Chandler:
OKAY, AND HE HASN'T
PROPOSED YET

443
00:18:02,498 --> 00:18:03,958
BECAUSE SHE HAS NO RING
ON HER FINGER.

444
00:18:03,958 --> 00:18:05,960
( gasping ):
WOW, YOU'RE GOOD.

445
00:18:05,960 --> 00:18:07,253
AFTER THIS, WE
SHOULD SOLVE CRIMES.

446
00:18:07,253 --> 00:18:08,755
YEAH.

447
00:18:08,755 --> 00:18:10,548
OKAY, GO-GO-GO GET HIM.

448
00:18:10,548 --> 00:18:13,175
OH, OKAY.

449
00:18:14,301 --> 00:18:15,428
EXCUSE ME, SIR.

450
00:18:15,428 --> 00:18:16,429
COULD YOU COME
WITH ME, PLEASE?

451
00:18:16,429 --> 00:18:18,932
YOU HAVE A PHONE CALL.

452
00:18:18,932 --> 00:18:19,933
WHO IS IT?

453
00:18:19,933 --> 00:18:21,225
IT IS YOUR OFFICE.

454
00:18:21,225 --> 00:18:23,143
DO YOU KNOW WHO
AT MY OFFICE?

455
00:18:23,143 --> 00:18:26,146
JOHN.
OH, JOHN. GREAT.

456
00:18:28,566 --> 00:18:30,359
HERE HE IS.
HI, HI.

457
00:18:30,359 --> 00:18:32,612
OKAY, THERE WAS A SLIGHT MIX-UP
AT THE JEWELRY STORE.

458
00:18:32,612 --> 00:18:34,363
THE RING YOU'RE
ABOUT TO PROPOSE WITH

459
00:18:34,363 --> 00:18:36,574
WAS SUPPOSED
TO BE HELD FOR ME.

460
00:18:36,574 --> 00:18:40,078
SO, I'M GOING TO NEED
TO HAVE THAT BACK...

461
00:18:40,078 --> 00:18:41,079
BUT IN EXCHANGE

462
00:18:41,079 --> 00:18:42,246
I'M WILLING
TO TRADE YOU

463
00:18:42,246 --> 00:18:45,792
THIS BEAUTIFUL,
MORE EXPENSIVE RING.

464
00:18:47,585 --> 00:18:48,586
WOW.

465
00:18:48,586 --> 00:18:50,463
I WOULD TRADE.

466
00:18:50,463 --> 00:18:51,756
IT IS BEAUTIFUL

467
00:18:51,756 --> 00:18:53,132
BUT I'M GOING TO
USE THIS ONE.

468
00:18:53,132 --> 00:18:54,467
NOW, IF YOU'LL
EXCUSE ME.

469
00:18:54,467 --> 00:18:56,052
NO, NO, SEE,
THIS IS MY FIANCEE

470
00:18:56,052 --> 00:18:58,304
AND HER HEART WAS SET
ON THAT RING.

471
00:18:58,304 --> 00:19:00,640
YOU DON'T WANT
TO BREAK HER HEART, NOW, DO YOU?

472
00:19:00,640 --> 00:19:04,560
YEAH, DO YOU WANT
TO BREAK A DYING WOMAN'S HEART?

473
00:19:04,560 --> 00:19:05,728
YOU'RE DYING?

474
00:19:05,728 --> 00:19:07,521
( coughing )

475
00:19:09,523 --> 00:19:11,525
YES, SHE'S DYING...

476
00:19:11,525 --> 00:19:13,987
OF A COUGH, APPARENTLY.

477
00:19:13,987 --> 00:19:15,446
Phoebe:
YES...

478
00:19:15,446 --> 00:19:17,782
AND IT IS MY DYING WISH
TO HAVE THAT RING.

479
00:19:17,782 --> 00:19:19,909
SEE, IF I'M NOT
BURIED WITH THAT RING

480
00:19:19,909 --> 00:19:22,244
THEN MY SPIRIT IS GOING
TO WANDER THE NETHERWORLD

481
00:19:22,244 --> 00:19:23,329
FOR ALL ETERNITY.

482
00:19:23,329 --> 00:19:26,040
OKAY, THAT'S ENOUGH,
